<h1>AI Tab Groups BETA — Privacy Policy</h1>
<p class="meta">Effective date: <time datetime="2026-11-03">2026-11-03</time>. Applies to the AI Tab Groups BETA browser
extension (beta).</p>

<h2>Summary</h2>
<p>AI Tab Groups BETA groups your browser tabs. Rule-based grouping runs entirely on your device. If you connect
your own AI provider, the extension sends limited tab <strong>metadata</strong> (not page contents) to
<strong>that provider</strong> to generate grouping suggestions. The extension has no developer-configured
data recipient — it contacts only the provider endpoint you enter.</p>

<h2>What the extension handles</h2>
<ul>
  <li><strong>Web browsing activity</strong> — the <strong>titles</strong> and the <strong>origin + path</strong>
  (site and path, without query strings or fragments) of tabs in your current window, used to group them and
  to build AI suggestions.</li>
  <li><strong>User-generated content</strong> — the <strong>names of your tab groups</strong> (text you
  created), sent as context for suggestions; and the <strong>grouping rules you create</strong> (match
  patterns and rule group names), which are stored and used <strong>locally only</strong> and are
  <strong>never sent</strong> to any provider.</li>
  <li><strong>Authentication information</strong> — the <strong>API key</strong> you enter for a chosen AI
  provider (required for cloud providers; a local provider may be configured without one).</li>
</ul>

<h2>How it is used and shared</h2>
<ul>
  <li>Rule-based grouping is performed <strong>locally</strong>; no data leaves your device for it.</li>
  <li>There are <strong>two</strong> explicit actions that send data, each <strong>only</strong> to the
  <strong>AI provider endpoint you configured</strong>:
    <ul>
      <li><strong>Test connection</strong> (Options) sends a short fixed test prompt and the model name, plus
      your API key in the authentication header if supplied — and <strong>no</strong> tab, group, rule, or
      page data.</li>
      <li><strong>Get suggestions</strong> sends the tab titles, origins/paths, and existing group names
      above, plus the fixed instructions and model name, with your API key in the authentication header, to
      return grouping suggestions.</li>
    </ul>
    The authentication header is provider-specific (<code>x-api-key</code> for Anthropic;
    <code>Authorization: Bearer</code> for OpenAI-compatible/local). Sending is separate from changing tabs:
    your tabs/groups change only when you <strong>Apply</strong> a suggestion.</li>
  <li>The extension sends requests <strong>only</strong> to the endpoint you enter; it has <strong>no
  developer-operated data sink</strong> in its code. Data you send goes to the third-party AI provider
  <strong>you</strong> selected, governed by <strong>that provider's</strong> privacy policy and terms.</li>
  <li>Your data is <strong>never sold</strong> and is <strong>not</strong> transferred to advertising
  platforms, data brokers, or for credit/lending purposes. The use of information received from Google APIs,
  and all use of user data, will adhere to the
  <a href="https://developer.chrome.com/docs/webstore/program-policies/user-data-faq">Chrome Web Store User
  Data Policy</a>, including the Limited Use requirements.</li>
</ul>

<h2>What is never sent</h2>
<p>Full URLs, query strings, and fragments; page text or other page content; your passwords or cookies; and
your locally-stored grouping rules. The extension does not read page contents.</p>

<h2>Local storage</h2>
<p>Your provider configuration and <strong>API key</strong>, your grouping rules, per-window cursor state,
and a short local diagnostics log are stored <strong>on your device</strong> in the extension's storage. The
diagnostics log never contains your key, URLs, paths, or tab titles.</p>
<p class="note">Your API key is stored as a plain value in local extension storage (no additional
encryption), and a local provider endpoint may use an unencrypted <code>http://localhost</code> connection; a
cloud provider is always reached over HTTPS. This is disclosed plainly for the beta.</p>

<h2>Your choices</h2>
<p>AI features are optional. You can remove the provider (which clears the stored key), edit or remove rules,
and uninstall at any time.</p>

<h2>Contact</h2>
<p>Questions about this policy: <a href="mailto:hello@georgediab.net">hello@georgediab.net</a>.</p>

